<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15747" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">encaustus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">encaut-</span></b> ), a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαυστος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>burned in</i>, <i>encaustic.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus pingendi,</span>”
				<i>the encaustic mode of painting</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 11, 41, § 149</span></i>
			; cf.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">, respecting it, O. Müller,
					Archäol. § 320: Phaëthon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 47, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">en-caustum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">encaut-</span></b> ), i., n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαυστον</span>, <i>the purple-red ink of
				the later Roman emperors</i>, Cod. Th. 7, 20, 1;
			August. contra Faust. 3, 18; <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1,
				23, 6 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
